WEBVTT

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:13.430
The AR Team splits up to
escape with the classified data.

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:14.930
"AR Team Griffin's elite T-Doll unit."
The AR Team splits up to
escape with the classified data.

00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:15.640
"AR Team Griffin's elite T-Doll unit."
Meanwhile, a new commander named Gentiane
encounters a Sangvis High-End Model.

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:20.850
"High-End Model Sangvis T-Dolls
with special powers and roles."
Meanwhile, a new commander named Gentiane
encounters a Sangvis High-End Model.

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:24.560
My name is Gentiane.
I was just assigned here today.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:26.230
"Gentiane A new Griffin commander."
My name is Gentiane.
I was just assigned here today.

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:27.650
"Gentiane A new Griffin commander."

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:31.190
Your first mission went well, it seems.

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:34.570
Well, it was the tutorial.

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:37.070
We are executing an emergency operation.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:40.740
The goal is to make contact
with and destroy Scarecrow,

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.540
and recover her memory module.

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:48.000
I was able to calculate it
just before the very end...

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:51.800
M4A1's coordinates.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:53.630
She's going to self-destruct!

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:56.180
Get out of there now, everyone!

00:00:56.180 --> 00:01:00.350
Now leave it to me and rest, Scarecrow.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:05.690
I'll find you... M4A1.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:10.190
"S09 Area, Coordinates: HVVQJ Sector"

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:29.710
Yes.

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:31.250
It's just me.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.840
Everybody is still at the rear.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:41.100
We've set a rendezvous point so
we can all retreat together, but...

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.350
Do you have the data?

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:46.270
Yes. It's in my possession.

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:49.940
Griffin's started a rescue mission.

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:52.110
Make contact with them, somehow.

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:55.150
All right.

00:01:55.150 --> 00:01:58.990
But Sangvis is close.
I need to be careful.

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:04.040
Be careful... code name... Sugar Cube.

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:05.410
Persica?

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:08.960
Sugar Cube?

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:47.720
Kryuger, the Sangvis appear to
have gotten the drop on us again.

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:54.940
You mean they found M4A1's
location before we did?

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:55.860
Yes.

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:59.360
We believe they may have a
doll that excels at hacking.

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:05.120
Or the information is leaking from inside.

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:10.370
Sir, everyone who works
for us can be trusted.

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:14.370
And the Dolls' security system is perfect.

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:18.420
Nothing is perfect, and no one
can be completely trusted.

00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:23.380
We can't even imagine what
they've got up their sleeves.

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:29.430
Just to be safe, we'll temporarily
call off your mission.

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:33.390
Then the mission to rescue AR Team...?

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:36.810
Of course, we'll continue it,
but in a different way.

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:42.280
By the way, Helian, does your
new commander like cats?

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:45.610
I've never asked...

00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:47.820
But probably she doesn't dislike them?

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:50.910
Kryuger, do you mean...

00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:52.080
Yes.

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:56.040
If we've hit a dead end,
we need to go back to basics.

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:01.670
No sign of the enemy.

00:05:01.670 --> 00:05:03.630
Strange.

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:06.260
There was that suspicious signal.

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:08.430
Are we wasting our time out here again?

00:05:08.430 --> 00:05:10.930
It's better if there are no enemies!

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:13.480
Let's head home!

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:16.230
Commander, this is FNC.

00:05:16.230 --> 00:05:19.360
We came to the signal's origin point,
but nobody's here.

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:20.860
What do we do?

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:21.860
Roger.

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:25.530
Check the area just to be safe, and if
there's nothing there, come home.

00:05:25.530 --> 00:05:27.950
Watch out for the enemy, okay?

00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:29.320
Okay.

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:31.580
We'll report if something comes up.

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:34.870
Eek!

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:37.120
--What?
--Nothing.

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:39.210
Just FN49 being her usual self.

00:05:39.210 --> 00:05:40.210
Bye!

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:42.920
FNC! A s-spider!

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:47.970
Watch out for the enemy?

00:05:47.970 --> 00:05:50.430
You sound like a mom.

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:51.470
Is that a problem?

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:52.850
We need to be careful.

00:05:52.850 --> 00:05:55.140
Yeah, but...

00:05:55.140 --> 00:05:59.850
Is what happened with
Scarecrow still bothering you?

00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:03.360
Repairs are all complete. It's not
good to keep thinking about it.

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:04.690
I know.

00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:07.610
I know.

00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:09.110
But still...

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.710
It seems you're doing a
good job with your missions.

00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:20.330
Well, I guess.

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:22.960
They're all things that I can do easily.

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:24.630
Getting bored?

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:26.340
No...

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:29.880
Then let me give you an important mission.

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:35.310
If you fail, Griffin will be destroyed,
and humanity will go extinct.

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:38.350
Why are you pressuring me like that?

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:41.770
M4A1.

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:43.860
A doll with 16LAB.

00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:45.650
16LAB?

00:06:45.650 --> 00:06:48.650
An organization that provides
technology to Griffin.

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:52.780
M4A1? What Scarecrow was talking about?

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:54.200
You remember, huh?

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:59.250
She made contact with Sangvis
during a mission in the S09 area.

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:01.540
She's gone missing.

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:04.040
I want you to find her before they do.

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:05.550
You want me to do that?

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:09.220
We're analyzing the coordinates
Scarecrow provided.

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:12.510
We'll contact you as soon
as they're available.

00:07:12.510 --> 00:07:17.810
Unfortunately, our main forces
can't help you fight Sangvis.

00:07:17.810 --> 00:07:19.430
I hate to ask, but this is up to you.

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:21.770
Ask the client for more details.

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:23.610
Client?

00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:26.480
The lead researcher at 16LAB.

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:32.450
Commander, this is Persica from 16LAB.

00:07:32.450 --> 00:07:34.370
Hello, hello.

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:36.330
Hello...

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:37.950
Why the cat ears?

00:07:37.950 --> 00:07:42.420
Persica developed the
technology the dolls use!

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:46.380
Oh, excuse me.

00:07:48.420 --> 00:07:50.090
Where are her shoes?

00:07:53.010 --> 00:07:56.600
Um, what did she mean by "client"?

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:01.690
I forgot my sugar cube.

00:08:03.230 --> 00:08:09.570
I had the AR Team recover
data my friend left behind.

00:08:09.570 --> 00:08:13.030
The Sangvis attacked them, though,

00:08:13.030 --> 00:08:14.820
and they were separated.

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:18.120
Have there been any reports since then?

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:21.450
Yesterday, actually.

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:22.910
Yesterday?

00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:29.050
It was short and hard to make out,
but I got a message from M4A1.

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:33.550
She's alone, but safe, it seems.

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:37.760
I told her Griffin was
working on a rescue.

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:41.140
Can you give us the coordinates
where she contacted you from?

00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:42.310
Of course.

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:47.360
Already cold.

00:08:48.690 --> 00:08:51.570
Kalina, look at this.

00:08:51.570 --> 00:08:56.450
This is the location where FNC
said she detected a strange signal.

00:08:56.450 --> 00:09:00.240
And this is where the message
Persica was talking about came from.

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:01.660
They're identical.

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:04.000
So she was there.

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:06.420
But why didn't she come out?

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:10.710
Maybe Persica hadn't fully
given her the info she needed?

00:09:10.710 --> 00:09:12.460
Maybe, but...

00:09:15.510 --> 00:09:16.510
Kalina...

00:09:16.510 --> 00:09:17.680
Yes?

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:23.270
Get me more data on M4A1--
no, the AR Team.

00:09:23.270 --> 00:09:26.190
Anything you can find. Everything.

00:09:26.190 --> 00:09:27.810
Everything?

00:09:27.810 --> 00:09:29.690
Well, okay.

00:09:29.690 --> 00:09:33.530
That's not really my job, though!

00:09:33.530 --> 00:09:35.030
Oh dear.

00:09:35.030 --> 00:09:37.410
Oh dear, oh dear.

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:38.740
Excuse me!

00:09:38.740 --> 00:09:41.530
MP5? What's wrong?

00:09:41.530 --> 00:09:46.790
Um, Kalina said you'd
been feeling down lately.

00:09:46.790 --> 00:09:48.210
That girl...

00:09:48.210 --> 00:09:50.210
Everybody else says the same thing.

00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:51.170
Everybody?

00:09:51.170 --> 00:09:54.130
Yes. FNC and P7, too.

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:57.180
That's not true, I think...

00:09:57.180 --> 00:09:58.260
Sorry.

00:09:58.260 --> 00:10:01.050
Commander, we're fine!

00:10:01.970 --> 00:10:04.270
We're T-Dolls.

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:08.520
And everybody in
Griffin, Helian, and Kalina

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:12.150
are working hard to let us
draw out our full strength!

00:10:12.150 --> 00:10:17.110
So please use us to complete your mission.

00:10:17.110 --> 00:10:18.990
Don't worry about us!

00:10:18.990 --> 00:10:21.870
We backup our memories!

00:10:21.870 --> 00:10:24.870
I'm me! MP5!

00:10:30.250 --> 00:10:31.460
Thank you.

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:47.430
Sorry, there were locks
on the AR Team's data.

00:10:47.430 --> 00:10:50.690
I can only get permission
for this training footage.

00:10:50.690 --> 00:10:51.940
That's plenty.

00:10:51.940 --> 00:10:54.150
So this is the AR Team?

00:10:54.150 --> 00:10:55.570
Yes.

00:10:55.570 --> 00:10:57.650
SOPII.

00:10:57.650 --> 00:10:59.780
AR15.

00:10:59.780 --> 00:11:01.280
M16.

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:06.660
And that's M4A1, their leader.

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:10.120
No heat signatures. Nothing on infrared.

00:11:10.120 --> 00:11:11.750
Nobody's in there.

00:11:11.750 --> 00:11:13.210
Let's just go in, okay?

00:11:13.210 --> 00:11:14.170
No.

00:11:14.170 --> 00:11:17.300
Nobody there doesn't mean nothing's there.

00:11:18.380 --> 00:11:20.470
What our leader says goes.

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:24.800
No change in air density.

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:26.060
Roger.

00:11:26.060 --> 00:11:27.350
Deploying map.

00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:31.440
Lobby in the middle. Hallway on the right.

00:11:31.440 --> 00:11:33.520
Vault dead ahead.

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:35.270
We're heading in.

00:11:41.740 --> 00:11:43.070
Clear!

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:54.540
Okay!

00:11:56.750 --> 00:11:57.750
Cl--

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:05.350
Clear, right?

00:12:09.140 --> 00:12:12.980
Oh, sorry. This is from
after their training.

00:12:12.980 --> 00:12:14.190
I'll stop it.

00:12:14.190 --> 00:12:15.730
No, let me see it.

00:12:18.860 --> 00:12:19.860
It's bitter!

00:12:19.860 --> 00:12:22.360
This has no milk or sugar!

00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:25.200
You should lay off the sweets.

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:27.870
You almost failed today's
training exercise.

00:12:27.870 --> 00:12:30.750
I already apologized!

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:32.910
Calm down, both of you.

00:12:32.910 --> 00:12:37.090
That's right. Don't cause problems for M4.

00:12:37.090 --> 00:12:38.040
It is bitter!

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:39.340
Right?

00:12:39.340 --> 00:12:42.010
You can use gun oil instead of milk.

00:12:42.010 --> 00:12:43.930
I can't drink that!

00:12:43.930 --> 00:12:48.300
--Well, bitter or not it's
better than gun oil.
--Hey, I can't drink that!
--Be quiet.

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:51.310
There were girls like this at school.

00:12:51.310 --> 00:12:54.980
Even while everybody else is
having fun, she's still watching,

00:12:54.980 --> 00:12:56.350
even the small stuff.

00:12:56.350 --> 00:12:59.900
And she's not easily influenced, either.

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:03.860
She's stubborn, in a way,
and won't give in when it counts.

00:13:03.860 --> 00:13:08.200
But she always puts others
first and herself last.

00:13:08.200 --> 00:13:11.490
I'm starting to see who M4A1 is.

00:13:14.460 --> 00:13:21.460
M4A1 didn't contact FNC's team because
she didn't want to get them involved.

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:27.180
M4A1 knew Sangvis
was after her, and close.

00:13:27.180 --> 00:13:32.770
It's probably the High-End Model that
Scarecrow contacted in her last message.

00:13:32.770 --> 00:13:37.060
If she joins up with other Griffin
dolls in this area, she'll stand out.

00:13:37.060 --> 00:13:40.070
And the High-End will be
more likely to catch her.

00:13:40.070 --> 00:13:43.690
She's capable of thinking
things through like that.

00:13:43.690 --> 00:13:47.610
But she can't avoid
making contact forever.

00:13:47.610 --> 00:13:52.700
A place where she can safely meet allies,
while watching out for enemies...

00:13:54.290 --> 00:13:59.130
Commander, Helian says she's
calculated the coordinates.

00:13:59.130 --> 00:14:02.550
Good timing. Put it on the map.

00:14:02.550 --> 00:14:03.920
Roger!

00:14:09.430 --> 00:14:12.430
I found you, M4A1!

00:14:14.100 --> 00:14:16.560
And there we go!

00:14:16.560 --> 00:14:18.190
That's the last of them, right?

00:14:18.190 --> 00:14:20.020
Let's check again.

00:14:20.020 --> 00:14:22.400
We should be careful!

00:14:22.400 --> 00:14:23.900
It'll be fine!

00:14:23.900 --> 00:14:27.950
Unless there's another Sangvis passing by.

00:14:27.950 --> 00:14:29.070
Wait!

00:14:29.070 --> 00:14:31.200
It's a powerful Sangvis signal!

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:32.160
They're close!

00:14:32.160 --> 00:14:34.040
What? Where?

00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:35.330
Tell me now!

00:14:35.330 --> 00:14:37.210
I'm right here!

00:14:37.210 --> 00:14:39.710
Hello, Griffin shitheads!

00:14:39.710 --> 00:14:41.380
It's a Sangvis shitboss!

00:14:41.380 --> 00:14:42.340
Damn it!

00:14:42.340 --> 00:14:43.800
We won't let you get away easily!

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:46.550
MG3, calm down!

00:14:46.550 --> 00:14:51.050
I don't even need to waste my time
with two low-powered dolls.

00:14:51.050 --> 00:14:53.470
I'm looking for a certain doll.

00:14:53.470 --> 00:14:56.220
Answer my questions, and I'll let you go.

00:14:56.220 --> 00:15:00.650
A girl with a stupid-looking face,
black hair, and an M4A1 carbine!

00:15:00.650 --> 00:15:02.230
You seen her?

00:15:02.230 --> 00:15:03.520
Black hair?

00:15:03.520 --> 00:15:04.980
Stupid-looking face?

00:15:04.980 --> 00:15:06.320
Never seen her.

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:10.200
So even with Griffin teams in
the area, she's still running?

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:14.490
She must be scared of me after all.

00:15:14.490 --> 00:15:17.620
I'm looking forward to seeing how much
longer you can keep running, M4!

00:15:20.960 --> 00:15:22.460
She left.

00:15:22.460 --> 00:15:24.790
What was she doing here?

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:29.760
MG3, something's bothering me.

00:15:29.760 --> 00:15:32.590
I think the doll the
commander is making us

00:15:32.590 --> 00:15:35.850
look for us is the same
one that boss is after.

00:15:35.850 --> 00:15:40.100
Yeah, but all we ran into
was a Sangvis recon team.

00:15:40.100 --> 00:15:41.850
You think this the wrong spot?

00:15:41.850 --> 00:15:46.190
Yes. She's not here,
but there should be a clue!

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:04.130
Looks like she ran this way.

00:16:08.170 --> 00:16:10.300
The bitch just won't stay put.

00:16:12.010 --> 00:16:13.220
Stop.

00:16:17.680 --> 00:16:20.270
She put up booby traps.

00:16:21.310 --> 00:16:23.140
We'll take a different route.

00:16:23.140 --> 00:16:26.820
Did you think I'd fall for
such a half-assed trap?

00:16:30.650 --> 00:16:34.530
That kind of accuracy with
an obsolete assault rifle?

00:16:37.620 --> 00:16:40.250
The traps were bait to lure us here?

00:16:40.250 --> 00:16:42.080
Get back! Leave the area!

00:16:44.830 --> 00:16:46.920
She reacted in time?

00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:50.050
Jaegers, back me up.

00:16:52.420 --> 00:16:53.720
I see.

00:16:53.720 --> 00:16:56.640
You were able to use the
terrain as part of a plan.

00:16:56.640 --> 00:16:59.470
You must have a command module.

00:16:59.470 --> 00:17:04.100
Explains how managed to
run for weeks, like a rat.

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:06.810
Sorry, but I've got a short temper.

00:17:06.810 --> 00:17:09.940
I'm not going to play your games.

00:17:09.940 --> 00:17:11.320
I'll fight with this,

00:17:11.320 --> 00:17:13.780
and this!

00:17:13.780 --> 00:17:19.330
I am Sangvis Ferri Product
ID SP524, Executioner!

00:17:19.330 --> 00:17:21.580
Can you stop me?

00:17:27.880 --> 00:17:30.210
How can she be so fast?

00:17:36.890 --> 00:17:40.060
Found you, M4A1.

00:17:43.680 --> 00:17:45.480
Let's have some fun!

00:17:52.360 --> 00:17:57.820
That idiot sacrificed
herself just to catch you.

00:18:02.450 --> 00:18:05.210
And to give me your coordinates!

00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:09.330
Don't disappoint me!

00:18:09.330 --> 00:18:11.460
Come on! Come on! Come on!

00:18:11.460 --> 00:18:12.750
Bring it!

00:18:20.260 --> 00:18:21.810
What's wrong?

00:18:21.810 --> 00:18:24.560
Show me your plan, Commander.

00:18:27.270 --> 00:18:28.730
Pathetic.

00:18:28.730 --> 00:18:32.650
You civilian dolls have
no real strength, huh?

00:19:02.430 --> 00:19:04.720
You Griffin shitdolls...

00:19:04.720 --> 00:19:07.560
You can't fight, so all
you do is set traps...

00:19:17.820 --> 00:19:21.610
You! Obsolete! Doll!

00:19:25.200 --> 00:19:28.410
Oops, I almost tore her apart.

00:19:28.410 --> 00:19:31.710
I have a lot of questions for you.

00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:34.040
Hey, stand her up.

00:19:34.040 --> 00:19:36.800
We'll take her arms and
legs off so she can't run.

00:19:39.840 --> 00:19:41.050
Hey!

00:19:44.510 --> 00:19:45.720
Sugar Cube.

00:19:52.980 --> 00:19:54.310
You!

00:19:54.310 --> 00:19:55.900
Don't move!

00:19:55.900 --> 00:19:57.360
You okay?

00:19:57.360 --> 00:19:59.900
You understood... good.

00:19:59.900 --> 00:20:03.990
Yes. The commander...

00:20:03.990 --> 00:20:05.120
How?

00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:09.040
How did the Griffin dolls find us?

00:20:09.040 --> 00:20:11.120
I told them...

00:20:11.120 --> 00:20:14.790
...that I'd lure you here to fight.

00:20:14.790 --> 00:20:18.090
And their commander gave them
the order to come here.

00:20:18.090 --> 00:20:19.800
When did you contact them?

00:20:19.800 --> 00:20:21.510
There was no message!

00:20:26.850 --> 00:20:29.180
It was a gamble.

00:20:34.020 --> 00:20:37.860
I hid a data disk and moved on.

00:20:42.070 --> 00:20:47.950
You were so focused on me that you didn't
try to keep track of what I'd been doing.

00:20:47.950 --> 00:20:53.500
You never thought about why
I was doing what I was doing.

00:20:59.210 --> 00:21:01.300
You never even imagined, did you?

00:21:01.300 --> 00:21:06.640
That obsolete civilian dolls would
notice details that you ignored,

00:21:06.640 --> 00:21:09.680
and their commander would
use that information

00:21:09.680 --> 00:21:13.060
to its fullest to give the perfect orders.

00:21:13.060 --> 00:21:17.520
That's the difference
between you and us, Griffin!

00:21:18.650 --> 00:21:22.070
So, what should we do to finish you off?

00:21:22.070 --> 00:21:23.530
Finish me off?

00:21:23.530 --> 00:21:26.200
Do you think it's over?

00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:32.120
If you're running to Griffin,
then there are things we can do, too.

00:21:32.120 --> 00:21:32.950
What?

00:21:32.950 --> 00:21:37.460
Your three friends are
still out there, right?

00:21:37.460 --> 00:21:42.590
You're safe, but what's
happening to them right now?

00:21:54.810 --> 00:21:59.610
Talking about my friends
was a mistake, Sangvis scum.

00:22:01.360 --> 00:22:03.360
It's fine.

00:22:03.360 --> 00:22:12.200
You know, you can't
get rid of us like... this...

00:22:16.370 --> 00:22:17.870
It's okay!

00:22:17.870 --> 00:22:20.460
Let's go home, M4A1!

00:22:20.460 --> 00:22:22.920
The commander is waiting!

00:22:22.920 --> 00:22:24.380
Commander...

00:22:29.890 --> 00:22:37.020
Big Sis M16... AR15, SOPII... I did it.

00:22:37.020 --> 00:22:38.520
Just wait for me.

00:22:44.610 --> 00:22:46.700
I won't abandon you.

00:22:46.700 --> 00:22:49.320
I'll save you all.

00:24:43.520 --> 00:24:46.940
Episode 4: "Silence 01."
